# Origin campus ERP — backend configuration
#
# Copy to .env and fill in. Everything except MONGODB_URI has a working
# default or degrades gracefully, so a fresh checkout runs with just that one.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored; this file is not. Never put a real secret in here.


# ─── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The only variable the app genuinely needs. Atlas: Connect → Drivers.
# Keep the credentials in the URI itself; there is no separate user/password
# setting (the MONGODB_USERNAME / MONGODB_PASSWORD pair some .env files carry
# is not read by any code).
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://USER:PASSWORD@cluster0.xxxxx.mongodb.net/?retryWrites=true&w=majority

# Which database inside the cluster. The URI above has no path, so this is
# what actually selects it.
MONGODB_DB=myDatabase


# ─── Server ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PORT=8000

# Allowed browser origin. Unset means "reflect whatever origin asks", which is
# fine locally; set it to the deployed frontend URL in production.
# CORS_ORIGIN=https://your-frontend.vercel.app

# "development" keeps the SIGINT/SIGTERM handlers that close the Mongo
# connection on shutdown. Leave unset on serverless, where the container is
# frozen and reused rather than terminated.
# NODE_ENV=development


# ─── Chatbot (Google Gemini) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Free key from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# Without it every reply is the canned "contact support" fallback — the bot
# still runs, it just never reaches the model. GEMINI_KEY is accepted as an
# alias for backwards compatibility.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Accepted as an alias for the above, for existing deployments that use it.
# GEMINI_KEY=


# ─── RFID attendance readers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shared secret the ESP32 gate readers send as the x-device-key header.
# Unset (the default) accepts scans unauthenticated, which is fine on a lab
# network but means anyone who can reach the server can mark attendance.
# Set it in production, and put the same value in the firmware's DEVICE_KEY.
# RFID_DEVICE_KEY=


# ─── Tests ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where `npm test` points its API contract tests. Those tests skip themselves
# when nothing is listening, so this is rarely needed.
# TEST_API_BASE=http://localhost:8000
